# Web Mobile Design System (`web/`)

Applies to all marketing and service pages under `web/src/app/`. Complements rules `20-design-system.mdc`, `51-web-production-gates.mdc`, and `60-zero-gate-health-check.mdc`.

## Viewport delegation (required)

Every public marketing page under `web/src/app/` **must** use `MarketingViewportGate` from [`web/src/components/marketing/MarketingViewportGate.tsx`](web/src/components/marketing/MarketingViewportGate.tsx) to split mobile (`< lg`) and desktop (`≥ lg`) layouts.

**Never** build bespoke mobile-only CSS modules that duplicate shared components. Mobile layout CSS extensions belong in `web/src/app/globals.css` under the `.home-mobile-marketing*` or `.service-detail-hero-mobile*` BEM namespaces.

## Service detail pages — shared mobile components

When adding or redesigning a service detail page, **reuse** these mobile components (do not reinvent):

| Section | Mobile component |
|---------|------------------|
| Hero | `ServiceDetailHeroMobile` |
| Section header | `MobileMarketingSectionHeader` |
| Feature/outcome grid | `MobileFeatureGrid` |
| Principle/why-build list | `MobilePrincipleList` |
| Process steps | `ProcessStepsMobile` |
| Pricing tiers | `EngagementTiersMobile` |
| FAQ | `ServiceFaqMobile` |
| Final CTA | `ProductLedFinalCTAMobile` |
| Workflow showcase | `AutomationWorkflowShowcaseMobile` (automation-specific) |
| Automation types | `AutomationTypesMobile` |

Gold-standard reference implementations:

- [`web/src/app/services/[slug]/page.tsx`](web/src/app/services/[slug]/page.tsx) — service page hub
- `/services/websites`, `/services/saas-applications`, `/services/ai-business-systems`

## Title accent gradient (required)

Section headings on marketing pages **must** use `titleLead` / `titleAccent` via `SectionHeading` or `MarketingAccentTitle`, which render the global `.marketing-title-accent` class.

The gradient is defined in `web/src/app/globals.css` (`.marketing-title-accent` and `.home-mobile-marketing__title-accent`).

**Never** override `.marketing-title-accent` in page-specific CSS modules. Per-page accent overrides break visual parity with other service pages.

## Desktop custom styling

Desktop-only visual treatments (cards, timelines, glass panels) may use scoped CSS modules **only when** they do not override global typography tokens or the title accent gradient. Mobile must still delegate to the shared components above.

## Desktop marketing layout discipline (required)

When building desktop card grids, timelines, or multi-column sections in `web/` marketing pages:

### Equal-height card grids

- Grid containers: `align-items: stretch` and `grid-auto-rows: 1fr` at each breakpoint where cards sit in a row.
- Card wrappers (`RevealItem`, grid children): `className="h-full"` when using motion wrappers.
- Card surfaces: `height: 100%`, `display: flex`, `flex-direction: column`.
- Footer CTAs / "Learn more" links: `margin-top: auto` so they align across rows regardless of body copy length.

### Process / timeline connectors

- **Never** use a single full-width pseudo-element line across an entire timeline row — it will overlap step labels and icons.
- Connect steps with **segment connectors** (`:not(:last-child)::after`) from circle center to next circle, positioned behind nodes (`z-index: 0`) with opaque node backgrounds + ring (`box-shadow`).
- Hide segment connectors on stacked/mobile single-column layouts.

### Cross-section visual rhythm

- Do not mix arbitrary card scales in adjacent sections (e.g. tiny icon tiles beside full feature cards) without explicit design intent.
- Pricing featured tiers: avoid `margin-top` offsets that break grid alignment — use grid `padding-top` for badge clearance instead.

## Audit before redesign

Before redesigning or adding a `web/` marketing/service page:

1. Read [`memories/repo/site-brain.md`](memories/repo/site-brain.md) — Marketing mobile system section
2. Audit an existing gold-standard service page in `web/src/app/services/[slug]/page.tsx`
3. Confirm mobile sections use `MarketingViewportGate` + shared `home-mobile-marketing` primitives
4. Confirm section headings use the global accent gradient (no per-page override)
5. Confirm desktop card grids use equal-height stretch + flex column + bottom-aligned CTAs
6. Confirm process/timeline connectors use segment lines behind nodes, not full-width overlaps
